  "notes": "West's heart lead has set up enough defensive tricks such that South cannot afford to lose the lead. South has only 6 tricks (2 spade tricks, the ♥A, 2 diamond tricks, and the ♣A). South will be able to make his contract if he can bring in the diamonds or clubs without losing a trick.\n\nBoth suits offer finessing possibilities. South should play the minors so as to combine his chances in both suits. South starts by cashing the ♦A and the ♦K. When the ♦Q drops, South has his 9 tricks and should cash them.\n\nIf the ♦Q does not drop, South can finesse East for the ♣K by playing dummy's high clubs through him. If East has the ♣K, South will have enough club tricks for the contract.",
